    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d153">

                <pb facs="0306" n="178" sameAs="frus:frus1928v01/pg178"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.60 i 12Anti-War/1: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Latvia</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Coleman</hi>)<anchor n="40"
                        xml:id="d153-f1"/>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Riga</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-09-04T16:00:00+02:00"><hi rendition="#italic">September 4,
                                1928—4 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received September 4—12:14
                        p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>72. Estonian Minister at Riga informed me yesterday that Estonia would adhere to
                    the Kellogg Peace Pact. Formal letter of adherence to follow.<anchor n="41"
                        xml:id="d153-f2"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Coleman</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d153-f1" n="40" type="source" xml:id="d153-f1-content">
                <p>The Minister in Latvia was also accredited to Estonia and Lithuania.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d153-f2" n="41" xml:id="d153-f2-content">
                <p>Law of adherence was voted by the Estonian Parliament Feb. 8, 1929, becoming
                    effective Feb. 25, 1929. Text transmitted to the Department in despatch No. 299,
                    Feb. 21, 1929, from the consul at Tallinn; not printed (file No. 711.60 i 12
                    Anti-War/12).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
